label: "ADR 0001: AtomicKeyspace, O(1) terminal reads, absent/incomplete taxonomy"
timestamp: "2026-08-21T10:51:16"
source: "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/path/docs/decisions/0001-atomic-keyspace.md"
references:
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-kernel-extension"
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-13-state"
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-08-dependency-boundary"
statement: >
  The kernel's keyed-I/O law, extended by human-ruled batches 1-9.
  Chosen: AtomicKeyspace with NO unconditional write anywhere on the
  module surface (create is put-if-absent, compare_exchange always
  carries If-Match, delete_if_match is the conditional delete-side
  dual); values live in envelope v2 {incarnation, version, payload} so
  CAS discriminates values AND eras structurally — tombstones witness
  deliberate destruction, incarnation counters fence cross-deletion
  ABA, certified trim certificates are the immutable retention floor,
  and lineage heads carry their own era stamp with conditional
  deletion tails (L9/L10/L14). O(1) terminal reads are two GETs with
  chain linkage below the terminal deliberately unverified; Absent,
  Destroyed, and StateHistoryIncomplete are distinct truths, never
  conflated. The application boundary is structural, not lexical:
  application crates cannot reach the adapter at all (KernelHandle +
  dependency floor) because a source token scan cannot prove
  capability absence. Rejected: any unconditional overwrite (reopens
  ABA), yeetz-sdk-core placement (dissolves the one-place assured
  contract boundary), lexical-only enforcement (three bypass classes
  compile clean), caller-discipline-only ABA safety. Measured fact
  (real-S3 probe, run 32423582844): Exoscale SOS etags are content
  hashes — the ABA case is REAL at the raw backend; the
  versioned/incarnated envelope is what closes it. Flips if: a backend
  changes etag semantics (the real-s3 probe rig re-measures and fails
  loudly), or a human rules the era model must move — a new ruling is
  a superseding vertex, never an edit here.
